--  What does not wait, handed to the hosted/system handle this provider
--  is built over, which events.ldn's `services` gives (D1363): the
--  environment, directories, the rest of the file system and terminals,
--  entropy and the wall clock.  Each entry is the system's, so a program
--  over this provider meets the same behaviour, errno and all, as one
--  over the system alone.  Running programs is programs.ldn's, which only
--  starts a child through the system (D479).

import core/io
import core/time

host is io.environment through services
host is io.directories through services
host is io.file_system through services
host is io.terminals through services
host is io.entropy through services
host is time.wall_clock through services
